Introcution:

- What we call JS is oneimplementation of a standard specification, called ECMAScript.
- ECMAScript 2015+ (also called ES6 and later) is the modern version of JavaScript. 
    It added new features that make coding cleaner, faster, and more organized.
    These include 
    - let/const for variables
    - arrow functions
    - classes
    - modules
    - template literals
    - destructuring
    - promises for async code
    - and new collections like Map and Set.